    "submission_id": "sub-invocation-ended-wording-1",
    "statement": "Correct the shared status/monitor wording when a provider invocation has ended but its stage is still running verification. Currently the frozen invocation duration can still be labelled \"running\". Work from admitted checkpoint ac17a5add7a58fcd845a8eee7485a633ef917de3 and preserve admitted task identity throughout.\n\nUse the existing shared interpretation and rendering paths. Distinguish an active invocation from a recorded ended invocation: the latter must have an honest duration label and must not imply that the stage or Job has completed, succeeded, or been accepted. Preserve active-invocation elapsed time, terminal-stage duration, Job age, provider/stage/Job deadlines and timeout causes. Preserve unknown, malformed, future, foreign-attempt and stale qualifications, the 15-second freshness rule, runtime details and worker-declared failure causes. Status, monitor and their shared viewer must agree. Add focused deterministic positive and negative coverage for active invocation, ended invocation with ongoing verification, terminal stage and missing/unqualified timing.\n\nScope is the narrow wording/interpretation correction and necessary deterministic tests under v12/python. No new collector or log parser; no telemetry-producer or scheduling-policy changes, publication optimization or unrelated fixes. Reuse existing CLI execution, schemas and activity sources. Run the required four-module verification supplied with this Job, plus appropriate focused tests. Record exact commands, counts, failures/skips and measured durations; distinguish simulated evidence from live-provider evidence.\n\nReturn a digest-bound candidate with base, changed paths, test evidence and remaining limitations for independent review. Do not import into the host or change live instances. Human integration and Git ownership remain separate. If a genuine clarification is needed, use the native handoff to the assigned reviewer and resume from the exact retained checkpoint; do not manufacture a question merely to exercise that branch."
  },
